# DOS Transit — the OPL2 demo, and a hybrid the hardware never was.
#
# Nine YM3812 voices and six YM2612 voices in one score. No machine
# ever shipped both, which is exactly why chipgen can: the AdLib's
# harder two-operator timbre carries melody and chords, the Genesis
# chip holds the low end where four operators actually buy something,
# and the DAC does the drums.
#
#   python3 python/chipgen.py examples/dos_transit.trk \
#       --opl-bank examples/opl_furnace_bank.json \
#       -o dos_transit.wav --profile
#
# The OPL patches come from Furnace's own library via
# python/opl_import.py. Everything named opl_* is built in, so this
# still renders without the bank — just with the generic voices.

title DOS Transit
author chipgen
game chipgen OPL2 demo
notes YM3812 + YM2612 + SN76489

# 24 ticks per row exactly — see tracker.py on why 192 would not do.
ticks 240
bpm 132
lpb 4

inst opl0 djtbmx_twinklekey
inst opl1 violin
inst opl2 chorus_organ
inst opl3 chorus_organ
inst opl4 opl_bell
inst fm0 deep_bass
inst fm1 strings
pan fm0 C
pan fm1 L

# 4.8 dB tremolo, 14 cents vibrato. Global to the chip, and only
# operators with their AM/VIB bit set hear it at all.
opldepth 1 1

mark intro
vol opl2 58
vol opl3 58
vol opl4 66
cols opl2 opl3 opl4 noise

